<title>USA: Parkvale Financial Q1 oper shr $0.57.</title>
<headline>Parkvale Financial Q1 oper shr $0.57.</headline>
<dateline>MONROEVILLE, Pa. 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended</p>
<p>							     September 30,</p>
<p>								1996     1995</p>
<p> Total interest income				$16,666 $16,561</p>
<p> Total interest expense				 9,737  10,073</p>
<p>   Net interest income				  6,929   6,488</p>
<p> Provision for loan losses				135     185</p>
<p>Net interest income after provision for losses</p>
<p>								6,794   6,303</p>
<p> Gain (loss) on sale of assets			    0	 0</p>
<p> Total other income					 519     510</p>
<p> FDIC special assessment				5,035     ---</p>
<p> Total other expenses				   3,530   3,521</p>
<p>  Income before income taxes			(1,252)   3,292</p>
<p> Income tax expense				     (464)   1,149</p>
<p> Net income						( 788)   2,143</p>
<p> Net income per share				 ( 0.19)    0.51</p>
<p> Dividend per share					0.13   0.104</p>
<p>NOTE: Net income for the Sept 30, 1996 quarter would have been $2.4 million or $0.57 per share up 11.1 percent from net income of $2.1 million or $0.51 per share for the quarter ended Sept 30, 1995, without the FDIC special assessment.</p>
<p>Parkvale reported a net loss for the quarter ended Sept 30, 1996 of $788,000 or $0.19 share as a direct result of the $5.0 million ($3.2 million, net tax) assessment.</p>
<p>All share amounts have been adjusted to reflect the 5-for-4 split paid on October 14, 1996.</p>
<p>Full company name is Parkvale Financial Corp,</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
